      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-go-arcadia-desktop/v0.1.0/data/screenshots/kde/1_running_config.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>The debugger's Video tab: every object the 8244 draws, with its position</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-go-arcadia-desktop/v0.1.0/data/screenshots/kde/2_debugger.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>The Controllers window: the membrane keyboard and both joysticks</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-go-arcadia-desktop/v0.1.0/data/screenshots/kde/3_controllers.png</image>
    </screenshot>
  </screenshots>
  <releases>
    <!-- The CURRENT release templates its version from @PROJECT_VERSION@, so
         it cannot disagree with the tree; past releases are literal. The
         release job checks that this first entry is still a template. -->
    <release version="@PROJECT_VERSION@" date="2026-11-02">
      <description>
        <p>
          The CONFIG client's start-up splash now shows the FujiNet logo. 0.1.0 embedded an earlier CONFIG whose logo was wrong.
        </p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.0" date="2026-11-01">
      <description>
        <p>
          First release: the Magnavox Arcadia 2001, Philips Videopac G7000 and Videopac+ G7400 transposed from MAME with the FujiNet Arcadia 2001 cartridge and an in-process FujiNet. CONFIG and FujiNet apps boot without a BIOS; games run on a BIOS you import. The membrane keyboard and both joysticks are on screen, and the debugger shows everything the 8244 knows. Needs Qt 6.7 or newer.
        </p>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
